{"Sprite", "", ApiKind::Table, "Sprite", "psxsplash API table."},
{"Sprite", "SheetIndex", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.SheetIndex(name)", "The sheet's index in the scene, or -1 when no sheet has that name."},
{"Sprite", "AnimIndex", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.AnimIndex(name)", "The animation's index, or -1 when none has that name. It searches every sheet and returns the first match, which is why the editor makes animation names unique across the scene."},
{"Sprite", "Create", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.Create(sheetName)", "Makes a sprite from a sheet and returns its id, 0 to 127. Returns -1 when the sheet does not exist or all 128 are in use. A new sprite is visible, on the screen plane at (0, 0), on layer 0, with a neutral tint, showing cell 0 and no animation."},
{"Sprite", "Destroy", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.Destroy(id)", "Frees the slot. The id may be handed out again by the next Create."},
{"Sprite", "SetPos", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.SetPos(id, x, y)", "Screen position of the sprite's top left corner, in whole pixels (-32768 to 32767)."},
{"Sprite", "SetWorldPos", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.SetWorldPos(id, x, y, z)", "Position on the world plane. The engine keeps it but does not draw world-plane sprites yet."},
{"Sprite", "BindToActor", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.BindToActor(id, actor, plane, offsetX, offsetY)", "Makes the sprite follow an object every frame. actor is an Actor.Find or Entity.Find handle; nil unbinds it. plane is 0 for the screen plane (the default) or 1 for the world plane; the offsets default to 0. On the screen plane the sprite's x is the object's X and its y the object's Z, in whole engine units, plus the offsets; the object's height is ignored. The bound position replaces whatever SetPos set."},
{"Sprite", "SetFrame", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.SetFrame(id, cell)", "Shows one cell of the sprite's sheet, 0 to 255, counted row by row from the top left, and drops the animation. The cell is not checked against the sheet's size."},
{"Sprite", "PlayAnim", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.PlayAnim(id, animName, restart)", "Plays an animation; the sprite switches to the animation's sheet. If the same animation is already playing it carries on, so calling this every frame is fine; pass true as restart to start it again from its first cell. An unknown name does nothing. Each cell shows for the animation's frame time in vsyncs, 60 a second of real time. A looping animation starts again after its last cell; otherwise it stops there."},
{"Sprite", "StopAnim", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.StopAnim(id)", "Stops the animation on the cell it is showing."},
{"Sprite", "SetFacingFromYaw", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.SetFacingFromYaw(id, firstAnimName, directions, yaw)", "For a character drawn from several directions: plays animation firstAnimName + n, where n (0 to directions - 1) is the direction nearest to yaw. The directional animations must follow one another in the sheet's list, starting with yaw 0 and going the way yaw increases. yaw is in pi-units like Entity.SetRotationY (1 = 180 degrees). Changing direction keeps the cell and timing, so a walk cycle does not restart, and keeps whether it is playing: call PlayAnim first. directions of 0 does nothing."},
{"Sprite", "SetVisible", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.SetVisible(id, bool)", "Hides or shows the sprite."},
{"Sprite", "IsVisible", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.IsVisible(id)", "Hides or shows the sprite."},
{"Sprite", "SetFlip", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.SetFlip(id, flipX, flipY)", "Mirrors the picture left to right and/or top to bottom."},
{"Sprite", "SetColor", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.SetColor(id, r, g, b)", "Tints the sprite, each 0 to 255. 128, 128, 128 is the picture's own colours; higher brightens, up to double."},
{"Sprite", "SetLayer", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.SetLayer(id, layer)", "Drawing order, 0 (front) to 11; a higher number is drawn as 11. All sprites are drawn in front of the 3D scene and behind UI canvases."},
{"Sprite", "SetSize", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.SetSize(id, w, h)", "Draws the cell stretched to w x h pixels. 0 for either keeps the cell's own width or height."},
{"Sprite", "SetIgnoreViewOffset", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.SetIgnoreViewOffset(id, bool)", "True pins the sprite to the screen, ignoring the view offset (for a score or a cursor)."},
{"Sprite", "SetViewOffset", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.SetViewOffset(x, y)", "A scroll for every sprite at once, in pixels: each one is drawn at its position minus this offset. Starts at 0, 0."},
{"Sprite", "GetViewOffset", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.GetViewOffset()", "A scroll for every sprite at once, in pixels: each one is drawn at its position minus this offset. Starts at 0, 0."},
{"Sprite", "Count", ApiKind::Function, "Sprite.Count()", "How many sprites exist."},
